# Component reduction for the nonabelian Section 13.5 branch

The normalizer deductions of 13.5.18–19 are proved from their explicit earlier
source inputs. Fitting centralization selects a genuine C-component of H,
with its actual star image and two-core quotient equivalence.

The proof of 13.5.20, the full component/module analysis of 13.5.21, and the
even noncentral chief-factor count in 13.5.22 remain assembly obligations.
The existing G.2.4 development supplies the order formulas, once 13.5.14
constructs its setup. This module does not assert those missing results or
Theorem 13.5.12.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.5.18–22, printed pp.922–924 (PDF pp.939–941).
-/
